. The item is an apple pie, but it's respelled as \"pi\" in celebration of <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pi_Day\">Pi Day</a>. Each year, it will appear in the Oak Depot on March 15 and be available for 7 days.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260903163011\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 55/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 61/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 7/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.007/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1019464/104857600 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   39.827      1 Template:Objects\n100.00%   39.827      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.9_prod_oaklands:pcache:idhash:2453-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timestamp 20260903163011 and revision id 17725. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>","categories":["Items","Decorative_Item","Events"],"links":[{"title":"The Oak Depot","exists":true}],"images":["Apple_Pi.png"]}
